---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../components/AdSlot.astro';
import { currentMonthYear } from '../utils/site-date';
import AppealLetter from '../components/AppealLetter.astro';
import AirportSidebar from '../components/AirportSidebar.astro';

const title = "Appeal Your Stansted Airport Drop-Off Charge | Free PCN Appeal Letter 2026";
const description = "Received a Stansted Airport drop-off charge? Use our free appeal letter to challenge your PCN.";
const canonical = "https://appealairportpcn.co.uk/stansted-drop-off-charge-appeal/";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "How to Appeal a Stansted Airport Drop-Off Charge",
  "description": "Step-by-step guide and free appeal letter template for challenging a Stansted Airport drop-off PCN.",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealPCN" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "AppealAirportPCN.co.uk" },
};

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much is the Stansted drop-off charge?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Since March 2026, Stansted charges £10 for up to 15 minutes. If you stay longer than 15 minutes, the charge is £28. The maximum stay is 30 minutes." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I appeal a Stansted drop-off charge?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Appeal to the operator using the instructions on your PCN. If your appeal is rejected, check whether the notice gives you access to POPLA." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is POPLA?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "POPLA is an independent appeals service for private parking charges. You normally need a POPLA verification code from the parking operator." }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "If I ignore the PCN will it go away?",
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Do not ignore it. The operator can take legal action to recover an unpaid charge." }
    },
  ],
};

const tips = [
  { heading: 'Do not pay while appealing', body: "Payment is treated as acceptance of the charge. Wait until both appeal stages are exhausted." },
  { heading: 'Note the time of day', body: "Stansted mornings are notoriously congested. If exit queues added time, say so explicitly." },
  { heading: 'Ask for the photos', body: "ANPR evidence request is a powerful move, errors in timestamps are surprisingly common." },
  { heading: 'POPLA is fully independent', body: "Operators must comply with POPLA rulings. It's free and unbiased." },
  { heading: '28-day deadline is firm', body: "After 28 days from the notice date, the formal appeal window closes." },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  currentPage="stansted"
  schema={[articleSchema, faqSchema]}
>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="breadcrumb">
        <div class="wrap"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/stansted-drop-off-charge-appeal/">Stansted</a></div>
      </nav>
      <h1>Appeal Your Stansted Airport Drop-Off Charge</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Stansted's drop-off zone is one of the most contested in the country, you have strong grounds to appeal. Our free template shows you exactly how.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <main>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="main-content">
        <div class="content-grid">

          <AirportSidebar current="Stansted Airport" tips={tips} />

          <div class="airport-main-column">
            <AppealLetter airport="Stansted Airport">
              <p>I appeal as the registered keeper of the vehicle. I am not obliged to identify the driver and decline to do so.</p>
              <p>1. APCOA cannot hold the registered keeper liable for this charge. The drop-off zone at Stansted Airport is on land under statutory control, including the Stansted Airport byelaws made under section 63 of the Airports Act 1986. The land is therefore not "relevant land" under paragraph 3(1)(c) of Schedule 4 to the Protection of Freedoms Act 2012 ("POFA"). The POFA keeper liability provisions do not apply, and APCOA has no lawful basis to pursue the registered keeper.</p>
              <p>2. This charge is not a byelaw penalty. It is a contractual parking charge, which can only be claimed from the driver. If the airport wished to enforce against keepers under its byelaws, that would be a matter for the airport. APCOA does not own the airport and has not said it acts under the byelaws. The Single Code of Practice (section 3.1.3, Note 2) says operators must not confuse the enforcement of byelaws with the contractual application of parking charges.</p>
              <p>3. The charge was not brought to the driver's attention before the contract was formed. Under Thornton v Shoe Lane Parking [1971] 2 QB 163, terms that are not brought to the other party's attention before the contract is made do not bind them. APCOA must show that the charge was clearly displayed before the vehicle entered the zone.</p>
              <p>4. The signage does not comply with section 3 of the Private Parking Sector Single Code of Practice. In particular:<br>
                - There was no entrance sign showing that terms apply and whether payment is required (3.1.1 and 3.1.2).<br>
                - The charge was not shown in a large, legible font (3.1.3(j) and 3.1.4).<br>
                - The signs could not be read on approach or in the lighting conditions (3.1.3(b) and 3.1.6).<br>
              Without clear terms shown before the driver committed to entering the zone, no valid contractual offer was made. APCOA is put to strict proof, with dated photographs, of the signs in place at the time.</p>
              <p>The registered keeper cannot be presumed or inferred to have been the driver, nor pursued under any interpretation of agency law. The Notice to Keeper can only hold the driver liable. Any reliance on Elliott v Loake would not assist: that was a criminal case decided on forensic and other evidence, not a presumption that the keeper was driving. APCOA has produced no evidence of who was driving.</p>
              <p>I require this PCN to be cancelled and ask for written confirmation.</p>
            </AppealLetter>

            <div class="instructions-card">
              <h2>How to use this appeal template</h2>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">1</div><div class="step-text">Click <strong>"Copy template"</strong> above, the full appeal is copied to your clipboard.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">2</div><div class="step-text">Log into the operator's online appeal system (or open your PCN) and paste the template into the appeal text box.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">3</div><div class="step-text">Submit and wait for a decision. The operator must respond within 35 days.</div></div>
              <div class="step-row"><div class="step-num">4</div><div class="step-text">If rejected, request your POPLA code and escalate to the free, independent adjudicator, operators lose the vast majority of cases on these grounds.</div></div>
            </div>

            <div class="airport-info-panel">
            <section class="intro-section">
              <h2>Stansted drop-off charge appeal</h2>
              <p>Got a PCN for dropping someone off at Stansted? It's highly likely you can cancel it. Use the free template above.</p>

              <h3>The charge</h3>
              <p>Stansted has one drop-off area, called the Express Set Down. It's on the terminal forecourt. Cameras read your number plate. There is no barrier.</p>
              <p>The rates have been, since 19 March 2026:
              <ul>
                <li>£10 for up to 15 minutes.</li>
                <li>£28 for 15 to 30 minutes.</li>
                <li>A maximum stay of 30 minutes.</li></p>
              <p>Before 19 March 2026 the rate was £7.</p>

              <h3>How you get a PCN</h3>
              <p>You don't pay by midnight the day after your visit. You pay online, by phone or through AutoPay.</p>
              <p>The PCN is £100. It drops to £60 if paid within 14 days.</p>

              <h3>Blue Badge</h3>
              <p>There is no exemption from the charge. Blue Badge holders can speak to a traffic marshal and get an extension to the 30-minute limit.</p>

              <h3>Free alternative</h3>
              <p>You can park for free for up to 60 minutes at the Mid Stay car park, with a shuttle to the terminal.</p> 
            </section>

            <section class="grounds-section sources-section">
              <h2>Sources</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>Stansted, <strong>Express Set Down Terms and Conditions</strong>: <a href="https://www.stanstedairport.com/terms-and-conditions/express-set-down/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.stanstedairport.com/terms-and-conditions/express-set-down/</a></li>
                <li>Stansted, <strong>Changes to Express Set Down</strong>: <a href="https://www.stanstedairport.com/communication-ticker-page/ticker-notice-4/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.stanstedairport.com/communication-ticker-page/ticker-notice-4/</a></li>
                <li>Stansted, <strong>Airport Byelaws</strong>: <a href="https://www.stanstedairport.com/about-us/byelaws/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.stanstedairport.com/about-us/byelaws/</a></li>
                <li>APCOA, <strong>Express Set Down payment information</strong>: <a href="https://stanstedairport-helpcentre.apcoa.com/hc/en-gb/articles/5319768229023-How-much-is-the-payment-and-when-is-it-required-by" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://stanstedairport-helpcentre.apcoa.com/hc/en-gb/articles/5319768229023-How-much-is-the-payment-and-when-is-it-required-by</a></li>
                <li>Protection of Freedoms Act 2012, <strong>Schedule 4</strong>: <a href="https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/9/schedule/4" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.legislation.gov.uk/ukpga/2012/9/schedule/4</a></li>
                <li>POPLA, <strong>Appeal guide</strong>: <a href="https://www.popla.co.uk/appeal-guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.popla.co.uk/appeal-guide</a></li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            </div>

            <div class="disclaimer">
              <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> AppealAirportPCN.co.uk is a free information resource for UK drivers. Nothing on this site constitutes legal advice. Templates are provided as a starting point, always review your specific circumstances. For complex cases, consider consulting a solicitor or Citizens Advice.
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

</BaseLayout>
